<title>GERMANY: Stark says wants all tradable Bonn debt in euro.</title>
<headline>Stark says wants all tradable Bonn debt in euro.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Juergen Stark, state secretary in the German finance ministry, said on Tuesday that he would recommend that all tradeable federal government debt be converted into the euro.</p>
<p>The move would not apply to German treasury bills, or &quot;schatzbriefe&quot;, and to financing treasury bonds, or &quot;finanzierungsschaetze&quot;, Stark said.</p>
<p>Stark was speaking at a news conference at the Bundesbank called to announce the issuance of a new strippable 30-year bond, at which he said earlier that he wanted all German debt to be converted into the euro in 1999 when the currency starts.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
